00:39:46.880 --> 00:39:51.300
Jim is apparently horrible at Call of Duty at the Stanford branch in this episode.
吉姆（Jim）在这一集中，在斯坦福分部玩《使命召唤》的表现显然很糟糕。

1004
00:39:51.300 --> 00:40:02.080
But in the episode, Email Surveillance, you can see in the background of the scene, at 20 minutes, 8 seconds, that Toby is playing Call of Duty on Jim's TV.
但在《电子邮件监控》那一集中，你可以在20分08秒的场景背景中看到，托比（Toby）正在吉姆的电视上玩《使命召唤》。

1005
00:40:02.580 --> 00:40:03.980
Remember at the barbecue, Jenna?
还记得烧烤派对吗，珍娜（Jenna）？

1006
00:40:04.140 --> 00:40:04.460
Yes.
记得。

1007
00:40:04.580 --> 00:40:04.780
Okay.
好的。

1008
00:40:04.960 --> 00:40:05.140
Yes.
是的。

1009
00:40:05.400 --> 00:40:14.100
So, and then also in Jim's bedroom at 15 minutes, 52 seconds, you can see an expansion pack of Call of Duty on Jim's desk.
还有，在15分52秒吉姆的卧室里，你可以看到吉姆的书桌上放着《使命召唤》的扩展包。

1010
00:40:14.360 --> 00:40:14.940
Come on.
得了吧。

1011
00:40:15.100 --> 00:40:16.040
Someone please explain.
谁来解释一下。

1012
00:40:16.620 --> 00:40:17.200
All right.
好吧。

1013
00:40:17.360 --> 00:40:17.700
Yes.
是的。

1014
00:40:17.720 --> 00:40:20.460
We actually had a lot of people write in about this glitch.
其实很多人写信来问这个漏洞。

1015
00:40:20.460 --> 00:40:23.700
I went to that time code, 15 minutes, 52 seconds.
我看了那个时间点，15分52秒。

1016
00:40:24.060 --> 00:40:24.980
There it is.
确实在那儿。

1017
00:40:25.100 --> 00:40:26.980
There is an expansion pack Call of Duty.
那里有个《使命召唤》的扩展包。

1018
00:40:27.860 --> 00:40:29.460
Here's how this went down, guys.
伙计们，事情是这样的。

1019
00:40:29.820 --> 00:40:38.800
Kent told me that the writers had a card up on the wall in the writer's room all through season two about a possible Call of Duty storyline.
肯特（Kent）告诉我，编剧们在第二季期间一直在编剧室的墙上贴着一张卡片，关于一个可能的《使命召唤》剧情线。

1020
00:40:38.900 --> 00:40:41.540
But they couldn't really ever figure out how to put it in.
但他们一直没想好怎么把它加进去。

1021
00:40:41.640 --> 00:40:45.100
And they had originally thought about doing something in email surveillance.
他们最初想在《电子邮件监控》里做点文章。

1022
00:40:45.900 --> 00:40:53.980
And if you remember, Angela, we did actually shoot some scenes where people were playing Call of Duty during Jim's party.
安吉拉（Angela），你还记得吗，我们确实拍了一些人们在吉姆的派对上玩《使命召唤》的场景。

1023
00:40:54.320 --> 00:40:54.480
Yeah.
是的。

1024
00:40:54.660 --> 00:40:56.120
But it wasn't a storyline.
但这并不是一个剧情线。

1025
00:40:56.580 --> 00:40:56.720
Yeah.
是的。

1026
00:40:56.800 --> 00:40:57.640
It wasn't a storyline.
那不是剧情线。

1027
00:40:57.640 --> 00:41:00.540
It was just something people were doing at the party kind of in the background.
那只是人们在派对背景里做的事情。

1028
00:41:00.540 --> 00:41:02.980
But that was there in the script.
但这确实在剧本里。

1029
00:41:03.700 --> 00:41:03.820
Yeah.
是的。

1030
00:41:03.960 --> 00:41:05.920
And it didn't really, though, go anywhere.
不过，它并没有真正发展成什么。

1031
00:41:06.580 --> 00:41:10.920
So finally, when they went to Stanford, they wrote this full plot line.
所以最后，当他们去斯坦福时，他们写了这个完整的情节线。

1032
00:41:11.380 --> 00:41:17.440
And they had to just live with the fact that there had been this tiny appearance of Call of Duty earlier.
他们只能接受之前有过《使命召唤》短暂出现过的事实。

1033
00:41:17.440 --> 00:41:23.800
But they so wanted a full Call of Duty story that they just went with it.
但他们太想要一个完整的《使命召唤》故事了，所以就这么做了。

1034
00:41:23.940 --> 00:41:25.600
I was like, it's worth it.
我当时想，这很值得。

1035
00:41:25.760 --> 00:41:26.120
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
是啊，是啊，是啊。

1036
00:41:26.220 --> 00:41:26.780
Whatever, whatever.
无所谓，无所谓。

1037
00:41:26.960 --> 00:41:27.520
Email surveillance.
《电子邮件监控》。

1038
00:41:27.720 --> 00:41:30.480
We've got to have a real episode that features Call of Duty.
我们得有一集真正以《使命召唤》为特色的剧集。

1039
00:41:30.780 --> 00:41:35.880
You know what I did for myself, the way I made it make sense is that Jim had roommates.
你知道我是怎么说服自己的吗？我让它变得合理的方式是，吉姆有室友。

1040
00:41:36.880 --> 00:41:37.280
You know?
你知道吗？

1041
00:41:37.580 --> 00:41:39.080
He had roommates who probably played it.
他有室友，他们可能玩这个游戏。

1042
00:41:39.200 --> 00:41:40.360
Maybe it was never his thing.
也许这从来都不是他的爱好。

1043
00:41:40.500 --> 00:41:40.940
You know?
你知道吗？

1044
00:41:41.160 --> 00:41:46.340
Maybe he stole the expansion pack and put it in his room to make his roommate stop playing.
也许他偷了那个扩展包放在自己房间里，好让室友别再玩了。

1045
00:41:46.940 --> 00:41:50.280
Maybe that's why it's in his room, along with his guitar that he never plays.
也许这就是它出现在他房间里的原因，和他那把从不弹的吉他放在一起。

1046
00:41:50.520 --> 00:41:52.640
OK, Jenna and Susie, come on.
好了，珍娜和苏西（Susie），得了吧。

1047
00:41:54.200 --> 00:41:54.840
Come on.
得了吧。

1048
00:41:55.100 --> 00:41:57.860
So I listened to the DVD commentary for this episode.
所以我听了这一集的DVD评论音轨。

1049
00:41:58.080 --> 00:42:02.580
And Jenna Rashida said that she got lessons on how to play Call of Duty from the writers.
珍娜·拉希达（Jenna Rashida）说她从编剧那里学了怎么玩《使命召唤》。

1050
00:42:02.740 --> 00:42:07.900
As soon as she got the job, they started teaching her how to play Call of Duty, which just cracks me up.
她一得到这份工作，他们就开始教她怎么玩《使命召唤》，这简直让我笑死。

1051
00:42:08.060 --> 00:42:10.920
And John actually had something really sweet to say in the commentary.
约翰在评论音轨里确实说了一些非常暖心的话。

1052
00:42:10.920 --> 00:42:17.140
He said that going to the Stanford branch, all of those actors had never worked together before, right?
他说去斯坦福分部的时候，那些演员以前从来没合作过，对吧？

1053
00:42:17.460 --> 00:42:23.160
And that playing Call of Duty with one another was actually a really fun icebreaker to get to know everyone.
而且一起玩《使命召唤》其实是一个非常有趣的破冰方式，能让大家互相了解。

1054
00:42:23.840 --> 00:42:27.220
You know, Ed and I traded some messages, and he said the same thing.
你知道，我和艾德互发了一些消息，他也说了同样的话。

1055
00:42:27.360 --> 00:42:30.300
He said they all played with the writers, and it was really, really fun.
他说他们都和编剧们一起玩，真的非常非常有意思。

1056
00:42:30.320 --> 00:42:33.760
And he told me that they also played for real on set.
他还告诉我，他们在片场也是真的在玩。

1057
00:42:34.580 --> 00:42:34.900
Yeah.
没错。

1058
00:42:35.140 --> 00:42:37.540
They were really playing during those scenes.
他们在拍那些戏份的时候是真的在玩游戏。

1059
00:42:37.600 --> 00:42:39.860
And then when they would cut, they would just keep playing.
而且导演喊停之后，他们还会继续玩。

1060
00:42:40.160 --> 00:42:42.920
He said it was a lot of fun, and people got super, super into it.
他说这很有趣，大家都玩得非常非常投入。

1061
00:42:43.800 --> 00:42:45.220
I have a little FOMO.
我有点错失恐惧症了。

1062
00:42:45.300 --> 00:42:48.920
I have a little FOMO about it, because I feel like we would have had fun with that at Scranton.
我对此感到有点错失恐惧，因为我觉得我们在斯克兰顿分部也会玩得很开心的。

1063
00:42:49.300 --> 00:42:49.860
I mean, all we...
我是说，我们当时……

1064
00:42:49.860 --> 00:42:52.000
See, we knew they were having fun over there without us.
你看，我们当时就知道他们在那里玩得很开心，没带上我们。

1065
00:42:52.320 --> 00:42:52.720
Dang it.
可恶。

1066
00:42:52.840 --> 00:42:54.660
All we were doing was playing solitaire.
我们当时只会玩纸牌接龙。

1067
00:42:55.440 --> 00:42:55.760
Exactly.
确实。

1068
00:42:55.760 --> 00:42:59.840
Oh, Jenna, did you get any scoop in your deep dive on who was the best player?
噢，珍娜，你在深入挖掘的时候有没有打听到谁是玩得最好的？

1069
00:43:00.080 --> 00:43:01.060
Who was our best player?
谁是我们那儿玩得最好的？

1070
00:43:01.620 --> 00:43:04.520
Well, I don't think any of the actors were very good.
嗯，我觉得演员里没几个玩得特别好的。

1071
00:43:04.980 --> 00:43:05.460
Oh, really?
噢，真的吗？

1072
00:43:06.020 --> 00:43:09.920
Ed said he didn't remember anyone being particularly great, including himself.
艾德说他不记得有谁特别厉害，包括他自己。

1073
00:43:10.600 --> 00:43:16.380
Kent told me that he was the best player when they started, but that during the editing phase
肯特告诉我，刚开始的时候他是玩得最好的，但在第一季的剪辑阶段，

1074
00:43:16.380 --> 00:43:22.260
of season one, when they were in Venice, co-producer Angie Hamilton was the best, hands down.
当他们在威尼斯时，联合制片人安吉·汉密尔顿绝对是玩得最好的。

1075
00:43:23.280 --> 00:43:27.860
But then, see, it sort of depends on who you ask, because Dean told me that during season
但你看，这取决于你问谁，因为迪恩告诉我，在第二季期间，

1076
00:43:27.860 --> 00:43:31.580
two, he and writer Mike Schur were the beSt.
他和编剧迈克·舒尔是玩得最好的。

1077
00:43:31.740 --> 00:43:33.000
They were at the top of the leaderboard.
他们当时在排行榜上名列前茅。

1078
00:43:33.120 --> 00:43:37.340
He said they got so into it that they took it over to Parks and Rec when they moved over
他说他们玩得太投入了，以至于后来转去《公园与游憩》剧组时，

1079
00:43:37.340 --> 00:43:40.160
there, and they played it every day on Parks and Rec.
他们把游戏也带过去了，每天都在那边玩。

1080
00:43:40.840 --> 00:43:46.840
And Kent did concur that Mike and Dean left as champions, but he also said that their assistant
肯特也承认迈克和迪恩离开时确实是冠军，但他还说他们的助理剪辑师，

1081
00:43:46.840 --> 00:43:49.060
editor, Mike Zurer, was pretty great.
迈克·祖勒，也相当厉害。

1082
00:43:49.940 --> 00:43:50.680
All right.
好的。

1083
00:43:50.860 --> 00:43:51.380
All right.
好的。

1084
00:43:51.380 --> 00:43:54.320
Well, I think those were fantastic questions.
嗯，我觉得这些问题问得太棒了。

1085
00:43:54.560 --> 00:43:56.280
Thank you so much, Shelby and Evan.
非常感谢你们，谢尔比和埃文。

1086
00:43:56.680 --> 00:43:56.860
All right.
好的。

1087
00:43:56.940 --> 00:43:59.900
So now at five minutes, 12 seconds, we're in the parking lot.
现在时间来到5分12秒，我们在停车场。

1088
00:44:00.040 --> 00:44:02.900
Dwight, you know, he's kind of psyching himself up like he does that.
德怀特，你知道的，他正在给自己打气，就像他平时那样。

1089
00:44:03.040 --> 00:44:05.060
We've seen him do this before, like in the stairwell.
我们以前见过他这样做，比如在楼梯间里。

1090
00:44:05.560 --> 00:44:10.180
And in the DVD commentary, Rain mentioned that that run that he does in the parking lot,
在DVD评论音轨里，雷恩提到他在停车场跑的那一段，

1091
00:44:10.300 --> 00:44:13.660
that Paul Lieberstein showed him exactly how he wanted that run done.
是保罗·里伯斯坦亲自演示给他看，让他一定要那样跑。

1092
00:44:14.480 --> 00:44:14.920
Really?
真的吗？

1093
00:44:15.160 --> 00:44:17.840
I picture these two guys just running back and forth.
我脑补了一下这两个大男人来回跑的样子。

1094
00:44:17.980 --> 00:44:19.660
It makes me laugh thinking about it.
想到这个我就想笑。

1095
00:44:19.660 --> 00:44:25.700
And then Dwight calls Jan and he says, hey, I need to talk to you.
然后德怀特给简打电话说，嘿，我需要跟你谈谈。

1096
00:44:25.840 --> 00:44:26.820
It's not safe here.
这里不安全。

1097
00:44:26.920 --> 00:44:27.880
He's crouching down.
他蹲了下来。

1098
00:44:28.160 --> 00:44:29.480
People are walking about.
周围有人走来走去。

1099
00:44:29.640 --> 00:44:30.280
Kevin's around.
凯文就在附近。

1100
00:44:30.280 --> 00:44:35.820
And he tells her to go to the Liz Claiborne outlet at exit 40 because he knows that she
他告诉她去40号出口的莉兹·克莱本奥特莱斯，因为他知道她

1101
00:44:35.820 --> 00:44:38.720
likes buying those blouses from Liz Claiborne.
喜欢买Liz Claiborne的那些衬衫。

1102
00:44:39.280 --> 00:44:39.680
Yeah.
是啊。

1103
00:44:39.820 --> 00:44:41.360
He says he'll meet her there.
他说他会在那儿见她。

1104
00:44:41.520 --> 00:44:41.700
Yeah.
是啊。

1105
00:44:41.700 --> 00:44:43.520
I'll meet you at the Liz Claiborne outlet.
我在Liz Claiborne折扣店等你。

1106
00:44:43.740 --> 00:44:45.260
He says, go in and shop.
他说，进去逛逛吧。

1107
00:44:45.420 --> 00:44:46.120
I'll meet you there.
我在那儿等你。

1108
00:44:46.260 --> 00:44:49.120
And she says, how do you know I like their blouses?
然后她说，你怎么知道我喜欢他们家的衬衫？

1109
00:44:49.120 --> 00:44:52.460
And he says, it's part of my job to know.
他说，了解这些是我的工作职责。

1110
00:44:52.760 --> 00:44:58.060
And then she has that great line where she's like, it literally is not part of your job.
然后她说了那句绝妙的台词，她说，这根本不是你的工作职责。

1111
00:44:58.360 --> 00:44:58.760
Yeah.
是啊。

1112
00:44:58.900 --> 00:45:01.740
He's like, it's absolutely not part of your job to know this.
他说，了解这些绝对不是你的工作职责。

1113
00:45:01.740 --> 00:45:06.460
And then Dwight's like noted how long, how long has Dwight been tracking her clothes?
然后德怀特说“记下了”，德怀特跟踪她的穿搭到底有多久了？

1114
00:45:07.000 --> 00:45:10.980
I feel like Dwight is the tracker the way we track things on the podcaSt.
我觉得德怀特就像我们在播客里追踪各种细节一样，是个追踪狂。

1115
00:45:10.980 --> 00:45:13.980
That's what Dwight was doing of like everyone in the office.
他当时就是在办公室里对每个人做这种事。

1116
00:45:14.280 --> 00:45:16.120
He's got some real creepy notebooks.
他有一些非常令人毛骨悚然的笔记本。

1117
00:45:16.440 --> 00:45:18.040
Oh, he has meticulous creepy notes.
噢，他有那种一丝不苟又令人毛骨悚然的笔记。

1118
00:45:18.640 --> 00:45:21.700
Lady, I had to do a deep dive the minute he said exit 40.
天哪，他一说40号出口，我就立刻去深挖了一下。

1119
00:45:22.020 --> 00:45:25.320
I had to know, are there Liz Claiborne outlets at exit 40?
我必须得知道，40号出口到底有没有Liz Claiborne折扣店？

1120
00:45:25.640 --> 00:45:27.720
So I can tell you all the outlets in Pennsylvania.
所以我可以告诉你宾夕法尼亚州所有的折扣店情况。

1121
00:45:27.920 --> 00:45:28.800
Did you go there, lady?
你去那儿了吗，女士？

1122
00:45:28.940 --> 00:45:29.700
Did you go there?
你去那儿了吗？

1123
00:45:29.700 --> 00:45:35.680
Okay, I did not go there, Angela, because remember when I said earlier that our fans
好吧，我没去，安吉拉，因为还记得我刚才说我们的粉丝

1124
00:45:35.680 --> 00:45:38.020
got real into some deep dives on this?
对这些细节深挖得很起劲吗？

1125
00:45:38.180 --> 00:45:44.540
We had multiple people write in about Liz Claiborne outlets and exit 40.
有好几个人写信告诉我们关于Liz Claiborne折扣店和40号出口的事。

1126
00:45:44.860 --> 00:45:50.380
Jenny Aguirre wrote in to say there is no exit 40, according to three Google Maps suggestions
珍妮·阿吉雷写信说，根据谷歌地图的三条路线建议，

1127
00:45:50.380 --> 00:45:51.780
from Scranton to New York.
从斯克兰顿到纽约根本没有40号出口。

1128
00:45:51.920 --> 00:45:52.820
Did you find that, Angela?
你查到了吗，安吉拉？

1129
00:45:53.120 --> 00:45:53.760
No exit 40?
没有40号出口？

1130
00:45:54.000 --> 00:45:55.940
Yeah, I couldn't find an exit 40 either.
是啊，我也没找到40号出口。

1131
00:45:55.940 --> 00:46:01.740
Okay, well, Michaela Brock said that the only Liz Claiborne store near Scranton is in Ramsey,
好吧，米凯拉·布洛克说斯克兰顿附近唯一的Liz Claiborne店在拉姆齐，

1132
00:46:01.860 --> 00:46:06.880
New Jersey, which is about an hour and 45 minutes away on the quickest route.
新泽西州，走最快的路线也要一个小时四十五分钟。

1133
00:46:07.120 --> 00:46:15.940
But Elizabeth M said that Jan has said she's been driving an hour, supposedly to New York
但伊丽莎白·M说，简曾说她开车要一个小时，据说是去纽约市，

1134
00:46:15.940 --> 00:46:21.900
City, which would not be on the way to this Liz Claiborne outlet that is in New Jersey,
那根本不在去这家位于新泽西州的Liz Claiborne折扣店的路上，

1135
00:46:21.900 --> 00:46:24.520
and it would actually add 25 miles to her drive.
而且实际上还会让她的车程多出25英里。

1136
00:46:25.140 --> 00:46:30.920
Well, I want you to know, when I was in junior high, my favorite perfume was the Liz Claiborne
好吧，我想让你知道，我上初中的时候，我最喜欢的香水就是Liz Claiborne

1137
00:46:30.920 --> 00:46:31.300
perfume.
香水。

1138
00:46:32.060 --> 00:46:32.460
Oh!
噢！

1139
00:46:32.720 --> 00:46:36.020
It came in a little, like, triangle, you know, and you took the top off.
它装在一个小小的，那种三角形的瓶子里，你知道的，把盖子取下来。

1140
